@cfriedt  Hi, I am very sorry but couldn't test it earlier. I am experimenting with `mdns_responder.c` and discovered that one of the reasons that avahi does not display the service could be that records are missing. Just for testing purposes I tried the following: I changed https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/39c535fef8347aa1850338e2ea8b3861b5203eef/subsys/net/lib/dns/mdns_responder.c#L389 to 
```
if (service_type_enum) {
				ret = dns_sd_handle_service_type_enum(record, addr4, addr6,
								      result->data, result->size);
				if (ret < 0) {
					NET_DBG("dns_sd_handle_service_type_enum() failed (%d)",
						ret);
					continue;
				}
				ret = dns_sd_handle_ptr_query(record, addr4, addr6, result->data,
							      result->size);
				if (ret < 0) {
					NET_DBG("dns_sd_handle_ptr_query() failed (%d)", ret);
					continue;
				}
			} else {
				ret = dns_sd_handle_ptr_query(record, addr4, addr6, result->data,
							      result->size);
				if (ret < 0) {
					NET_DBG("dns_sd_handle_ptr_query() failed (%d)", ret);
					continue;
				}
			}
```
As from that moment avahi-discover started displaying my device properly with all additional fields. I know this is probably not the fix but this did however learn me that avahi discover is expecting additional fields or query responses.  Avahi is probably waiting until the additional query is replied before displaying the service.

Furthermore I discovered that there seems to go something wrong during query extraction. The first query (dns_sd_handle_service_type_enum) seems to be handled well as can be monitored in wireshark. However the second query to ._zephyr._tcp.local seems to cause errors.  I'm not sure why or what is wrong.

```
